E AX3040 352-tyvar-delegation.ax:42:5-12 result-only-tyvar "`conjure` returns type variable `a`, which no parameter mentions, and its body produces that result rather than never returning: the caller chooses the type and a `cast` fabricates the value" ?"three ways out: return a concrete word type and let callers write `cast`; or make it DIVERGE, so every path ends in a call that never returns, which is what makes `for all a` honest; or tag the declaration `;@axiom:raw` to put it in the unsafe layer on purpose"
E AX3040 352-tyvar-delegation.ax:53:5-10 result-only-tyvar "`sneak` returns type variable `a`, which no parameter mentions, and its body produces that result rather than never returning: the caller chooses the type and a `cast` fabricates the value" ?"three ways out: return a concrete word type and let callers write `cast`; or make it DIVERGE, so every path ends in a call that never returns, which is what makes `for all a` honest; or tag the declaration `;@axiom:raw` to put it in the unsafe layer on purpose"
E AX3040 352-tyvar-delegation.ax:58:5-10 result-only-tyvar "`mixed` returns type variable `a`, which no parameter mentions, and its body produces that result rather than never returning: the caller chooses the type and a `cast` fabricates the value" ?"three ways out: return a concrete word type and let callers write `cast`; or make it DIVERGE, so every path ends in a call that never returns, which is what makes `for all a` honest; or tag the declaration `;@axiom:raw` to put it in the unsafe layer on purpose"
E AX3073 352-tyvar-delegation.ax:44:4-8 undeclared-unsafe "`conjure` forges `a` out of `Int` with `cast`, and its declaration does not say so" #"forges a reference" ?43:1:"write `;@axiom:effect(unsafe)` above the declaration"~>";@axiom:effect(unsafe)\n" ?"this fires where the unsafe operation is performed, not up the call chain. The tag alone makes the declaration a trusted encapsulation, whose callers inherit nothing; write `;@axiom:precondition(...)` beside it as well when its safety depends on what its caller passes. If the operation is not wanted here the fix is to stop performing it, not to stop saying so"
E AX3073 352-tyvar-delegation.ax:63:6-10 undeclared-unsafe "`mixed` forges `a` out of `Int` with `cast`, and its declaration does not say so" #"forges a reference" ?60:1:"write `;@axiom:effect(unsafe)` above the declaration"~>";@axiom:effect(unsafe)\n" ?"this fires where the unsafe operation is performed, not up the call chain. The tag alone makes the declaration a trusted encapsulation, whose callers inherit nothing; write `;@axiom:precondition(...)` beside it as well when its safety depends on what its caller passes. If the operation is not wanted here the fix is to stop performing it, not to stop saying so"
